{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470569-wonders-background-cost","id":1470569,"title":"Wonders background cost","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-15T18:12:11-08:00","id":1470569,"title":"Wonders background cost","content":"I know there are some threads that discuss this topic and maybe it doesn't have a definitive answer, but it doesn't hurt to try.<br /> <br /> M20 has this table in the background section about wonders as well as in the toybox that says each dot of wonder background gives 1-3 wonder points. This means a wonder with a lvl 5 sphere effect would cost 4 background points, if the wonder points are double the highest sphere lvl and 2 background points, if the ratio is 1:1. Note that the wonder background doesn't have the $ symbol to show that the background cost is doubled.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/KGdLXkt/Smart-Select-20211215-174534-Moon-Reader-Pro.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Now, after this table in the toybox section, we have the descripiton of a wonder with a lvl 4 sphere effect costing 8 background points (actually 9 because it has +1 in Arete), which means wonders should cost highest sphere lvl effect x2 in background points.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/wRmsfmz/Smart-Select-20211215-175219-Moon-Reader-Pro.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> So, we have 4 options for a lvl 5 effect wonder:<br /> <br /> A) Costing 2 background points, which is ridiculously low, but makes sense according to the table<br /> B) Costing 4 background points, which makes more sense, but we have no reason to think that since it's a mixture of both table and description<br /> <br /> C) Costing 8 background points, being another mixture of both table and description, meaning that you get the doubled wonder cost from the table (10 points), see how much dots it costs (4) and then double it.<br /> <br /> D) Costing 10 background points, following the description and slmost all the examples provided by M20, but ignoring the table<br /> <br /> So, I ask now: is there any official FAQ somewhere explaining this? What you think is the right way to calculate it?<br /> <br /> I believe option D is the most used and accepted. On this ase we should just throw the table away?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 12-15-2021, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T01:43:28-08:00","id":1470589,"title":"","content":"Perhaps this helps:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/708948-how-do-wonders-work-in-m20?p=710466#post710466\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/708948-how-do-wonders-work-in-m20?p=710466#post710466\"> How do wonders work in M20? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/708948-how-do-wonders-work-in-m20?p=710466#post710466\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/708948-how-do-wonders-work-in-m20?p=710466#post710466 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Hello to all I was reading M20 on wonder and background cost and i found this on page 328 Okay i said, maybe is there as to not mess a character sheet with 6+ background dots. As many wonders in previous editions went for 7+ dots. So now a 7+ wonder would be represented in a 4 point background. Simple </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T04:10:52-08:00","id":1470607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470569-wonders-background-cost?p=1470589#post1470589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps this helps:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/708948-how-do-wonders-work-in-m20?p=710466#post710466\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/708948-how-do-wonders-work-in-m20?p=710466#post710466\"> How do wonders work in M20? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/708948-how-do-wonders-work-in-m20?p=710466#post710466\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/708948-how-do-wonders-work-in-m20?p=710466#post710466 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Hello to all I was reading M20 on wonder and background cost and i found this on page 328 Okay i said, maybe is there as to not mess a character sheet with 6+ background dots. As many wonders in previous editions went for 7+ dots. So now a 7+ wonder would be represented in a 4 point background. Simple </div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Ambrosia, thank you for your answer. But it kinda doesn't, because the table says freebie and experience, not just experience.<br /> <br /> PS: How buying a wonder with xp works? Shouldn't the char find or build a wonder and in this case why the hell spend xp?<br /> Unless you just spend xp and the ST suddenly puts a eonder in the char way, which would be kinda lame if not done properly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T06:29:47-08:00","id":1470619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470569-wonders-background-cost?p=1470607#post1470607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> PS: How buying a wonder with xp works? Shouldn't the char find or build a wonder and in this case why the hell spend xp?<br /> Unless you just spend xp and the ST suddenly puts a eonder in the char way, which would be kinda lame if not done properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the M20 rules I believe that making your own Wonder (including Trinkets and Charms) costs xp. One xp per 5 quintessence spent to make the Wonder if I'm not mistaken, so I believe crafting a level 5 Wonder would cost 25+ quintessence and 5+ xp. If making Wonders did not cost XP, then any player character with Prime 4 would win the game by crafting multiple Wonders for every effect they can manage. They would use their Wonders for everything and therefore never take Paradox and when the Wonder burned out from the Paradox, they would just discard it and use the next, or craft another.<br /> <br /> Finding a Wonder (being given a Wonder by the ST) of course does not cost xp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T07:49:35-08:00","id":1470630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>breggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470569-wonders-background-cost?p=1470619#post1470619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By the M20 rules I believe that making your own Wonder (including Trinkets and Charms) costs xp. One xp per 5 quintessence spent to make the Wonder if I'm not mistaken, so I believe crafting a level 5 Wonder would cost 25+ quintessence and 5+ xp. If making Wonders did not cost XP, then any player character with Prime 4 would win the game by crafting multiple Wonders for every effect they can manage. They would use their Wonders for everything and therefore never take Paradox and when the Wonder burned out from the Paradox, they would just discard it and use the next, or craft another.<br /> <br /> Finding a Wonder (being given a Wonder by the ST) of course does not cost xp.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're wrong. Book of Secrets p.151<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because a mage who creates a Wonder must invest it with energy, and has to go through all of the other necessary steps described below, a player does not have to spend experience and/<br /> or Background points to obtain a Wonder that the mage herself has created. The given costs are for items that have been obtained from sources, rather than for Wonders crafted by the mage. </div> </div> </div>Built wonders do not cost xp, but they cost the time, effort, possibly dox and quintessence to create them, depending on the wonder type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T11:11:15-08:00","id":1470646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470569-wonders-background-cost?p=1470607#post1470607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PS: How buying a wonder with xp works? Shouldn't the char find or build a wonder and in this case why the hell spend xp?<br /> Unless you just spend xp and the ST suddenly puts a eonder in the char way, which would be kinda lame if not done properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Buying Backgrounds for xp was always a polemical thing. Rules allow it, but in general I see it makes more sense to just gain and loose them in the story (finding/building) - and charging xp for these things would be supremely bizarre (like, a character found a magic want but no xp? Can't use it. Weird. It becomes more so if you can't meet people, make friends, or buy property that will aid you w/o expending xp).<br /> <br /> The second case (<i>you just spend xp and the ST suddenly puts a wonder in the char</i>) offers some potential. It could be understood as the character expending downtime to, say, do some favors to a Master in exchange for a Wonder. Instead of, say, expending time hitting the books to learn that extra dot of Sciences or training Martial Arts. Ultimately, it's abstracted growth that happens mostly off camera in all cases<br /> <br /> I wouldn't use this, but if I did that's how.<br /> <br /> As for the rest:<br /> <br /> I'm not 100% sure if this helps or makes things worse, but I think there's some wordplay there between &quot;dots&quot; and &quot;points&quot; there.<br /> <br /> As you note, the book says &quot;that 4 dot Arete 5 Talisman then...&quot; .This indicates that there's a difference between the Background &quot;dots&quot; and the amount of &quot;points&quot; they actualy cost. Dots and points aren't the same.<br /> <br /> It get's worse because it clearly could be interpreted that buying a Wonder with freebies costs <i>more</i> than with the points you're given to buy Backgrounds (weird, because Bacground points cost 1 = 1 with freebies).<br /> <br /> But if we make the logical jump to say that freebies and Background points are the same since they cost the same, I think that maybe one can make some sense of this (and why the example costs 10 points)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Toybox</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">An individual Wonder <u>can have up to one separate power for each <b>dot </b></u>in that Background. A three-dot Wonder, for instance, can have up to three different powers, although many three-dot Wonders have only one or two abilities. <u>Because each Wonder uses Sphere-based Effects, those <b>dots </b>depend upon the Sphere Rank</u> of the object\u2019s most powerful Effect. A Talisman, for instance, that uses a Forces 4/ Prime 4 Effect would be a four-dot Background, its Arete Trait as high as 4.<br /> ...<u>for one extra Background <b>point</b>, that four-dot Talisman could have an Arete of 5</u>...</div> </div> </div> </div>My interpretation: Sphere &amp; Effects &quot;cost&quot; <b>dots</b>, not points. Extra Arete costs <b>points </b>instead<br /> <br /> Hence: A Wonder with a 4th level effect it's a 4 dot wonder. And a 4 dot Wonder <i><b>can </b></i>cost from 10 to 12 xp/freebies/background points. Because that variable number of points it's what the 4th dot costs. If we err to the minimum, it would have an Arete of 4 and cost 10 points. It could have an extra Arete added for one extra <i>point </i>(now it costs 11 points) that's not going to change the amount of dots the Background shows (it's still a 4 dot Talisman)<br /> <br /> It's similar as how the amount of Effects a wonder has doesn't get reflected in the cost, only the amount that it <i>could</i> have (except this time it *does* cost you something to increase the value to the maximun). If that wonder had Arete 8 instead, it would cost 13 points and would figure as 5 dots Wonder in the sheet<br /> <br /> Does this mean that the dots on the sheet reflect little about the <i>real </i>value and power of a Wonder? Yes, yes it does. It isn't a very nice interpretation, but it's all I got","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-16-2021, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T12:12:04-08:00","id":1470650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470569-wonders-background-cost?p=1470646#post1470646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the rest:<br /> <br /> I'm not 100% sure if this helps or makes things worse, but I think there's some wordplay there between &amp;quot;dots&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;points&amp;quot; there.<br /> <br /> As you note, the book says &amp;quot;that 4 dot Arete 5 Talisman then...&amp;quot; .This indicates that there's a difference between the Background &amp;quot;dots&amp;quot; and the amount of &amp;quot;points&amp;quot; they actualy cost. Dots and points aren't the same.<br /> <br /> It get's worse because it clearly could be interpreted that buying a Wonder with freebies costs <i>more</i> than with the points you're given to buy Backgrounds (weird, because Bacground points cost 1 = 1 with freebies).<br /> <br /> But if we make the logical jump to say that freebies and Background points are the same since they cost the same, I think that maybe one can make some sense of this (and why the example costs 10 points)<br /> <br /> <br /> My interpretation: Sphere &amp; Effects &amp;quot;cost&amp;quot; <b>dots</b>, not points. Extra Arete costs <b>points </b>instead<br /> <br /> Hence: A Wonder with a 4th level effect it's a 4 dot wonder. And a 4 dot Wonder <i><b>can </b></i>cost from 10 to 12 xp/freebies/background points. Because that variable number of points it's what the 4th dot costs. If we err to the minimum, it would have an Arete of 4 and cost 10 points. It could have an extra Arete added for one extra <i>point </i>(now it costs 11 points) that's not going to change the amount of dots the Background shows (it's still a 4 dot Talisman)<br /> <br /> It's similar as how the amount of Effects a wonder has doesn't get reflected in the cost, only the amount that it <i>could</i> have (except this time it *does* cost you something to increase the value to the maximun). If that wonder had Arete 8 instead, it would cost 13 points and would figure as 5 dots Wonder in the sheet<br /> <br /> Does this mean that the dots on the sheet reflect little about the <i>real </i>value and power of a Wonder? Yes, yes it does. It isn't a very nice interpretation, but it's all I got</div> </div> </div> </div>As usual, your answer is of great quality. That's a nice explanation you gave there.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the dots and points are off by one. A wonder with a 4th lvl effect is a 4 dots wonder and costs 8 points. The example says 9 because of the +1 in Arete.<br /> By your logic the table should be:<br /> <br /> \u2022 1-3 points<br /> \u2022\u2022 4-5 points<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 6-7 points<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 8-9 points<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 10+ points<br /> <br /> Because the explanation and examples made clear that each dot costs 2 points.<br /> <br /> Also, how would that work? I spend 4 background point that gives me 4 dots in Wonder background, which gives a pool of 10-12 points to get wonders?<br /> <br /> How much background/freebies would one have to spend to get a lvl 5 sphere effect wonder with the regular 5 Arete?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T13:32:28-08:00","id":1470656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470569-wonders-background-cost?p=1470630#post1470630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're wrong. Book of Secrets p.151<br /> <br /> Built wonders do not cost xp, but they cost the time, effort, possibly dox and quintessence to create them, depending on the wonder type.</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand corrected. But as I've come to expect from perusing this forum, your response is so blunt and unpleasant that I will not make the mistake of responding to any of your posts again. Thank you for teaching me a lesson.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T13:52:08-08:00","id":1470657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>breggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470569-wonders-background-cost?p=1470656#post1470656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I stand corrected. But as I've come to expect from perusing this forum, your response is so blunt and unpleasant that I will not make the mistake of responding to any of your posts again. Thank you for teaching me a lesson.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My apologies. It was not my intention to offend you by any means. I was just stating the fact that you're post wasn't right according to RAW. Not being an english native speaker might influence my answers.<br /> Any answer is very welcomed to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T15:32:51-08:00","id":1470662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470569-wonders-background-cost?p=1470657#post1470657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My apologies. It was not my intention to offend you by any means. I was just stating the fact that you're post wasn't right according to RAW. Not being an english native speaker might influence my answers.<br /> Any answer is very welcomed to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>In almost every language it is considered unpleasant to state directly to someone that they're wrong. You sometimes come out as aggressive because of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T16:40:54-08:00","id":1470667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470569-wonders-background-cost?p=1470650#post1470650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As usual, your answer is of great quality. That's a nice explanation you gave there.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the dots and points are off by one. A wonder with a 4th lvl effect is a 4 dots wonder and costs 8 points. The example says 9 because of the +1 in Arete.<br /> By your logic the table should be:</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that does seem to be the assumption in a lot of places, like in the Gadget creation rules of BoS. The Alanson Hardswit does cost 8 points and it's a 4 dot's wonder. If that cost refered to the points given per level, it would be a lvl 3 Wonder in it's most basic form (7-9). But it's not just that one, IN general book assumes Wonder costs like a double cost background, ignoring the whole freebie/xp part of the table, and ignoring that the Background it's never - ever -marked with a $. Couldn't find that exact example you mention in my M20 after that Toybox table, though - curious, but it does seem to follow.<br /> <br /> It's all very confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-16-2021, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T17:55:18-08:00","id":1470675,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> In my language it only means you are wrong and that's it. Nothing aggresive about that. It can be aggressive if you speak in an aggressive manner.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470569-wonders-background-cost?p=1470667#post1470667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that does seem to be the assumption in a lot of places, like in the Gadget creation rules of BoS. The Alanson Hardswit does cost 8 points and it's a 4 dot's wonder. If that cost refered to the points given per level, it would be a lvl 3 Wonder in it's most basic form (7-9). But it's not just that one, IN general book assumes Wonder costs like a double cost background, ignoring the whole freebie/xp part of the table, and ignoring that the Background it's never - ever -marked with a $. Couldn't find that exact example you mention in my M20 after that Toybox table, though - curious, but it does seem to follow.<br /> <br /> It's all very confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alason Hardswit seems to be an exception. Maybe because it has several powers, much more than the 4 it supposed to have. Maybe it's an example of how wonders can go out of the creation rules.<br /> <br /> About the lvl 5 wonder, how much you believe it should cost in background/freenies points according to your undestanding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T19:19:21-08:00","id":1470681,"title":"","content":"More like according to my <i>lack </i>of understanding, :P. Probably you're rigth in that the most acceptable answer it's the D) as it's the one that's being used in almost every example (albeit it does ignore the general rule). A rule can tolerate a few exceptions, but when nearly everything it's an exception one may start to think the rule was worded wrongly. So, I think that's the most canon-ish.<br /> <br /> I would rule 5 points, though. That's what ordinary &quot;lvl 5&quot; Wonders costed in older editions, and if M20 isn't going to bother being clear about costs I see not why change. Wonders can be very powerful, but they can be stolen or targeted. There's a risk/reward situation. I think that's fine.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T07:24:02-08:00","id":1470709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470569-wonders-background-cost?p=1470681#post1470681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I would rule 5 points, though. That's what ordinary &quot;lvl 5&quot; Wonders costed in older editions, and if M20 isn't going to bother being clear about costs I see not why change. Wonders can be very powerful, but they can be stolen or targeted. There's a risk/reward situation. I think that's fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't find a good definitive source of revised cost for wonders, but iirc, it's 1 point for each effect lvl (so a wonder with a Prime 5 and Forces3/Prime 2 effect would cost 8 points) +1 for every 5 quintessence, +/- merits and flaws. Can you confirm that?<br /> <br /> Can't remember how Arete goes into that math.<br /> <br /> Also, I can't confirm this with FbdF. Shuriken glove is a single Forces 3/ Prime 2 effect and 5 quintessence but costs 5 points. It should be 4...<br /> <br /> Your 5 points lvl 5 wonder must be a single effect or as much as 5, like in M20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T11:44:58-08:00","id":1470724,"title":"","content":"Wonder rules change a lot between books, and aren't particularly clear in any edition. And you can imagine examples that contradict the rules are going to be present (to be fair, Rotes sometimes contradict the general rules of magick). Idealy, one would want to call these &quot;exceptions&quot; - but for that they need to be less than the normal.<br /> <br /> Revised Core it's very fuzzy about the limitations, it even says that the level of the Wonder and that of the Background don't need to correspond.<br /> <br /> FbdF it's, in my opinion, the best book about Wonders yet. But it's far from perfect.You have a more complex system that varies depending on the type of the Wonder - which makes a lot of sense since wonders of different types have different capabiliters, and contemplates stuff like - say - than a Wonder with one Effect and a Wonder with two Effects shouldn't cost the same. On the other hand the layout of the book isn't great and mixes a lot of fluff with crunch. Also, the examples sometimes seem wierd - like that one you mention, it doesn't seem to correspond with the rest - and the system isn't always clear.<br /> Relevant examples of these systems:<br /> p.20: An Artifact point value it's equal to the Sphere ratings of all it's Effects; double this total for Artifacts with continuous Effects (+/- flaws, merits or Paradox handling).<br /> p.48: Talisman ... point cost is equal to their Arete plus 1 point per (extra?) Effect plus 1 point per 5 Quintessence they can store.<br /> <br /> If the +1 point per Effect ain't talking about <i>extra </i>Effects, then the ONLY Talisman that has the cost right it's the Shuriken Glove. But I want to give them a generous reading and say the wording it's about <i>adding </i>Effects, and the Gloves are the exception or a typo (or maybe it has something I'm not seeing...).<br /> <br /> Personaly, my understanding it's that the Background taken at level 5 as allowing a single level 5 Effect Wonder for sure, or a combination of lower levels that add up to 5 - but more than that could be negotiable at ST discretion. That's what I've used in the past. Perhaps there's other Revised systems I'm not familiar with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-17-2021, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T14:01:06-08:00","id":1470740,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> Older editions rules are as confusing as M20, if not more. I believe the p.20 entry means the sum of all effects? So a wonder with Prime 5 effect and a Forces3/Prime2 effect would cost 8?<br /> <br /> Anyway, after reading and thinking a lot and talking to people I believe I managed to understand how the system works without ignoring neither the table nor the explanation. And your insight about the difference between dots and points helped a lot.<br /> <br /> Ok, first, there are 3 different counting systems. Let's call them, for clarification:<br /> <br /> - background points: the pool of points you get to spend in wonder cost. Each freebie/background you spend in the background Wonder, gives you about 1-3 background points as per the table.<br /> <br /> - Wonder rating: How many dots a wonder has. Regularly it equals wonder arete (arete can be increased) and highest sphere lvl effect. It gives a notion on how powerful a wonder is.<br /> <br /> - wonder cost: the cost of each wonder with background points from the pool. The cost follows the description I posted in OP. So, wonder cost= highest sphere lvl x2 + any increase in Arete.<br /> <br /> Now, you spend your background/freebies points to get dots in the wonder background. According to the table, you get about 1-3 background points per dot. You spend that pool of background points buying wonders, that costs their wonder cost.<br /> <br /> It's actually simple after you get the concepts. So, in my OP example, the wonder rating 5 have 10 wonder cost and needs 10 background points, which you get by buying 4 dots in the background. So option B was right.<br /> <br /> Note that wonder has no $ and is not a doubled background. I always thought wonders were very expensive. A lvl 5 costed 10 freebies, that's a lot for an item that someone can break. It happens it costs 4 freebies. That's a lot better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T07:41:37-08:00","id":1470934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470569-wonders-background-cost?p=1470657#post1470657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My apologies. It was not my intention to offend you by any means. I was just stating the fact that you're post wasn't right according to RAW. Not being an english native speaker might influence my answers.<br /> Any answer is very welcomed to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries. Your answer caught me off guard and possibly in a poor mood. I'm over it and I rescind my assertion that I won't respond to your posts. I apologize also for being too quick to get annoyed.<br /> <br /> To continue, I really thought there were parts of the Book of Secrets that indicate an XP cost to make Wonders, but on quick review I couldn't find it. I haven't had the time to read more carefully.<br /> <br /> That said though, I don't necessarily think it's a bad idea for an ST to require a small xp cost - at my group's table we make the other requirements easier (time, materials, quintessence) since gathering those are disruptive to the game unless they are part of the story and can involve all characters. But making those requirements easier means that a small xp cost offsets it so that a mage can't just load up on a bunch of Wonders for essentially free.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T18:30:00-08:00","id":1470974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>breggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470569-wonders-background-cost?p=1470934#post1470934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No worries. Your answer caught me off guard and possibly in a poor mood. I'm over it and I rescind my assertion that I won't respond to your posts. I apologize also for being too quick to get annoyed.<br /> <br /> To continue, I really thought there were parts of the Book of Secrets that indicate an XP cost to make Wonders, but on quick review I couldn't find it. I haven't had the time to read more carefully.<br /> <br /> That said though, I don't necessarily think it's a bad idea for an ST to require a small xp cost - at my group's table we make the other requirements easier (time, materials, quintessence) since gathering those are disruptive to the game unless they are part of the story and can involve all characters. But making those requirements easier means that a small xp cost offsets it so that a mage can't just load up on a bunch of Wonders for essentially free.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No problem, my friend.<br /> <br /> You were kind of right, because I think previous editions indeed required a xp cost.<br /> Well, lowering other requisites might worth the xp points, for some players, depending on the history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T19:37:59-08:00","id":1470979,"title":"","content":"Revised edition had an XP cost for backgrounds. First and second editions did not. 20th anniversary edition pointed this out and included XP costs for those who want to use them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T07:57:47-08:00","id":1471011,"title":"","content":"I'm personally in favor of XP costs for Backgrounds, but also with the Sanctity rules in place (if the story strips you of a BG, then you get refunded full cost). Had applied that on my games even before CoD gave it a name.<br /> <br /> But I also don't think every thing that can be represented by a BG should be so, it only defines who has primary control over the thing, the Player or the ST.<br /> <br /> That said, I think a mixed approach is valid. A player that wants the Wonder enough to invest XP should have an easier time getting it and some sense of being secure in its possession (the Player, not the Character). For an item the player won't spend XP on, then the ST is free to make it as hard or easy to get it as the story demands and do with it afterwards as they please.<br /> <br /> Yet, I think in general Wonder Creation rules have always been more complex than they really need to. In the end the rules only govern putting into it effects the Mage can already cast, so as useful as they are, they're not going to really add new powers to the Mage. And even for a Mage who don't have access to those effects, a Wonder is far more static than actually saving the XP for personal growth. The other lines have far less juice out of their magic systems and yet work perfectly fine with simpler and cheaper magic items, Mage is so complicated to get something that really doesn't give you a fraction of the benefits.<br /> <br /> My personal preference today is to ditch completely the rules for Wonders in any edition and adapt the rules for Imbued Items and Artifacts from Mage the Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T11:55:37-08:00","id":1471022,"title":"","content":"Yeah. One of the things that I have on my M5 wishlist is for the Wonder rules to be simplified, streamlined, and \u2014 in terms of how wonders are to be made \u2014 folded into the rules for extreme Feats. <br /> <br /> And I would definitely borrow some ideas from Awakening, such as the Imbued Items rules or the \u201csufficiently powerful Magick costs XP to perform\u201d concept found in <b>Imperial Mysteries</b>: generalizing the concept, practically permanent Effects, or even Effects that are so big that they'll have lasting consequences on the world at large long after the Effect itself has technically ended, shouldn't just be a matter of how many Successes are needed; there should be precious resource costs, such as specific kind of Tass and/or XP, associated with such \u201cgreat works\u201d. Not to restrict the Magick per se, but rather as a way of encouraging story: if a working requires you to use a particular kind of Tass, then you must somehow acquire that Tass; and unless you already have a ready supply of it, that involves going out and finding it. <br /> <br /> You <i>should</i> be able to model feats such as shifting a Reality Zone using the Magick rules: not because shifting a Zone should be something that can be done with just a series of dice rolls, but because the Magick-working game systems should incorporate narrative-driven elements into large works. Riffing off of Clarke's Law, a sufficiently powerful Magick should be indistinguishable from Story. <br /> <br /> And making Wonders should be an application of that, not a separate game system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T15:57:44-08:00","id":1471045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470569-wonders-background-cost?p=1471022#post1471022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a sufficiently powerful Magick should be indistinguishable from Story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Poetic. Couldn't have said it better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-22T08:09:06-08:00","id":1471087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470569-wonders-background-cost?p=1471022#post1471022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would definitely borrow some ideas from Awakening, such as the Imbued Items rules or the \u201csufficiently powerful Magick costs XP to perform\u201d concept found in <b>Imperial Mysteries</b>: generalizing the concept, practically permanent Effects, or even Effects that are so big that they'll have lasting consequences on the world at large long after the Effect itself has technically ended, shouldn't just be a matter of how many Successes are needed; there should be precious resource costs, such as specific kind of Tass and/or XP, associated with such \u201cgreat works\u201d. Not to restrict the Magick per se, but rather as a way of encouraging story: if a working requires you to use a particular kind of Tass, then you must somehow acquire that Tass; and unless you already have a ready supply of it, that involves going out and finding it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Requiring special Tass it's a good idea. FbDF <i>almost </i>does this. It does have systems about the materials and Tass needed for the Wonder, but then it only gives a bonus. And some of that can be created with simple magick. So, it ain't that relevant in the end - but it has the rigth spirit.<br /> <br /> Imperial Mysteries definitely does arch-magic rigth. I believe that what makes that system great, more than anything else, it's Quintessence. Quintessence isn't a random resource you get over time. Quintessence it's a story. It's mistery that, by it's unique nature and it's relation to the spell, very much causes the spell to become a story. You're literally fueling your spells with story.<br /> <br /> Let's keep that in mind...<br /> <br /> Making things cost XP in the current state of the game will not encourage story because XP you will get over time, regardless of the kind of story you're playing. XP main purpose isn't to encourage story but to regulate character grow rate. On the contrary, I don't like Backgrounds costing XP <i>precisely </i>because, as things are now, it <i>dis</i>incentivizes story: If you need a Cult, instead of roleplaying, roll those social attributes, etc. you're entitled to pay the XP you won in the last Technocratic raid<br /> <br /> Now, I know the ST should ban that expenditure unless the player did something to justify it, but the fact it's that typically XP is expended taking in count off-camera &quot;downtime actions&quot; (because nobody want's to- say- have to roleplay studying STEM all day to gain Sciences. It's not going to be an important part of the story). ST can policy this, but it's a negative solution. I would rather not move the story with the ban hammer.<br /> <br /> However, the way XP is <i>rewarded </i>does encourage story in a more positive way. An easy and concrete example being the &quot;mystical xp&quot; that Awakening rewards from discovering misteries. That encourages players to seek that kind stuff, moving stories foward (oWoD uses XP to encourage story too, but in a more general fashion). The key here it's not so much how XP is expended, but how it's gained<br /> <br /> If Wonder making requires an XP gained in a particular kind of story, or a story that has a specific elements in the plot, that does encourage to include such stories or plot elements. For instance: The story where you got the special Tass. Special Tass and special XP could be related (or even be the same thing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-22-2021, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T03:00:54-07:00","id":1476563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470569-wonders-background-cost?p=1470740#post1470740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> Older editions rules are as confusing as M20, if not more. I believe the p.20 entry means the sum of all effects? So a wonder with Prime 5 effect and a Forces3/Prime2 effect would cost 8?<br /> <br /> Anyway, after reading and thinking a lot and talking to people I believe I managed to understand how the system works without ignoring neither the table nor the explanation. And your insight about the difference between dots and points helped a lot.<br /> <br /> Ok, first, there are 3 different counting systems. Let's call them, for clarification:<br /> <br /> - background points: the pool of points you get to spend in wonder cost. Each freebie/background you spend in the background Wonder, gives you about 1-3 background points as per the table.<br /> <br /> - Wonder rating: How many dots a wonder has. Regularly it equals wonder arete (arete can be increased) and highest sphere lvl effect. It gives a notion on how powerful a wonder is.<br /> <br /> - wonder cost: the cost of each wonder with background points from the pool. The cost follows the description I posted in OP. So, wonder cost= highest sphere lvl x2 + any increase in Arete.<br /> <br /> Now, you spend your background/freebies points to get dots in the wonder background. According to the table, you get about 1-3 background points per dot. You spend that pool of background points buying wonders, that costs their wonder cost.<br /> <br /> It's actually simple after you get the concepts. So, in my OP example, the wonder rating 5 have 10 wonder cost and needs 10 background points, which you get by buying 4 dots in the background. So option B was right.<br /> <br /> Note that wonder has no $ and is not a doubled background. I always thought wonders were very expensive. A lvl 5 costed 10 freebies, that's a lot for an item that someone can break. It happens it costs 4 freebies. That's a lot better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am trying to get my head around this, but I am coming up short.<br /> <br /> So I want to have a watch that makes me immune to time by pressing it. Thats a Time 5 power.<br /> <br /> The talisman having a Time 5 sphere power, which means it has to be a 5 point wonder with 5 arete. Yes?<br /> <br /> How many background points does it cost? If it\u2019s just doubled, that would be a 5-point wonder costing 10 freebies?<br /> <br /> But then, the table says 13-15?<br /> <br /> I need to be led through this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T08:10:45-07:00","id":1476579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470569-wonders-background-cost?p=1476563#post1476563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am trying to get my head around this, but I am coming up short.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is that for this rule <b><i>Background Point</i></b> =/= <b><i>Background Dots</i></b>. This is probably the most accurate understanding of the rules, but also o means the rules are written with a poor choice off words. For easing this, lets call them instead <b><i>Wonder Points</i></b>.<br /> <br /> So each Background <b>DOT</b> you have (bought directly or with Freebies) gives you 1-3 <b><i>Wonder Points</i></b>. Those are the points you use to build your Wonder.<br /> <br /> A Talisman with a Time 5 effect has <i>at least</i> Arete 5 and is worth at least 10 <b><i>Wonder Points</i></b>. Those are not <i>Freebies</i> or dots, they are bought with dots instead, so this says nothing <i>directly</i> about the Wonder rating.<br /> <br /> Your maximum amount of <b><i>Wonder Points</i></b> at 3 dots is (from 1-3 per dot) 9, so it isn't possible to build this wonder as rating 3. Instead, this Wonder would have to be 4 or 5, possibly with some small bonus effect using the remaining <b><i>Wonder Points</i></b> if any.<br /> <br /> Which rating between 4 and 5, and how many <i><b>Wonder Points</b></i> exactly you get out of them is up to the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T09:25:04-07:00","id":1476585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470569-wonders-background-cost?p=1476579#post1476579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is that for this rule <b><i>Background Point</i></b> =/= <b><i>Background Dots</i></b>. This is probably the most accurate understanding of the rules, but also o means the rules are written with a poor choice off words. For easing this, lets call them instead <b><i>Wonder Points</i></b>.<br /> <br /> So each Background <b>DOT</b> you have (bought directly or with Freebies) gives you 1-3 <b><i>Wonder Points</i></b>. Those are the points you use to build your Wonder.<br /> <br /> A Talisman with a Time 5 effect has <i>at least</i> Arete 5 and is worth at least 10 <b><i>Wonder Points</i></b>. Those are not <i>Freebies</i> or dots, they are bought with dots instead, so this says nothing <i>directly</i> about the Wonder rating.<br /> <br /> Your maximum amount of <b><i>Wonder Points</i></b> at 3 dots is (from 1-3 per dot) 9, so it isn't possible to build this wonder as rating 3. Instead, this Wonder would have to be 4 or 5, possibly with some small bonus effect using the remaining <b><i>Wonder Points</i></b> if any.<br /> <br /> Which rating between 4 and 5, and how many <i><b>Wonder Points</b></i> exactly you get out of them is up to the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do I reconcile it with this part of the book then?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because each Wonder uses Sphere-based Effects, those dots depend upon the Sphere Rank of the object\u2019s most powerful Effect. A Talisman, for instance, that uses a Forces 4/ Prime 4 Effect would be a four-dot Background, its Arete Trait as high as 4. </div> </div> </div>Pg 653 M20 core<br /> <br /> As far as I can interpret, this would mean that to have an arete 5 talisman, I would need it to be a 5 dot background for the wonder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T21:35:40-07:00","id":1476629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470569-wonders-background-cost?p=1476585#post1476585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do I reconcile it with this part of the book then?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't, didn't you read the entire conversation? The rules on Wonders are all over the place and have never been completely coherent not even in the same core book, pick whatever Mage core book you want.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3153_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3153\" data-vbnamecard=\"3153\">Lord Revan</a> did his best to come up with a sensible interpretation that takes the most of M20 into consideration, but this is just a huge mess all around. Also his interpretation accounts for most actual examples of Wonders.<br /> <br /> If you look for the sample Wonders in the core and supplements, you'll see lots and lots of sample cases that do not follow the paragraph you quoted. And those are the canonical stuff for players to get or make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-18T21:02:26-07:00","id":1476702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1470569-wonders-background-cost?p=1476585#post1476585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do I reconcile it with this part of the book then?<br /> <br /> <br /> Pg 653 M20 core<br /> <br /> As far as I can interpret, this would mean that to have an arete 5 talisman, I would need it to be a 5 dot background for the wonder.</div> </div> </div> </div>You reconcile by acknowledging that they used a poor choice of words. If they cslled that wonder points, sll would mske sense.<br /> <br /> If you just consider the text, where wonder cost is higest level sphere x2 a 5 rating wonder would cost 10 background points. And all the three tables present on M20 and Book of Secrets would make absolutely no sense.<br /> <br /> To make the best interpretation of all the texts and tables, you need to consider they didn't used the right words intheir explanation. <br /> I couldn't find a logic where everything they said fit and I'm open to see one.<br /> <br /> Answering your question, as monteparnas said, your wonder would cost 4 background points","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}